.TH str_ndup 3
.SH NAME
str_ndup \- duplicate up to n characters of a string
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "str.h"
.PP
.BI "char *str_ndup(const char *" s ", size_t " n ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B str_ndup
allocates a new memory block and copies at most
.I n
characters from string
.I s
into it, ensuring the result is null-terminated. The caller is responsible for
freeing the returned pointer.
.SH SEE ALSO
malloc(3)